# Clean Code Guidelines

## Constants Over Magic Numbers

- Replace hard-coded values with named constants
- Use descriptive constant names that explain the value's purpose
- Prefer `src/lib/constants.ts` for shared product limits (tiers, caps)

## Meaningful Names

- Variables, functions, and classes should reveal their purpose
- Names should explain why something exists and how it's used
- Avoid abbreviations unless they're universally understood

## Smart Comments

- Don't comment on what the code does — make the code self-documenting
- Use comments to explain **why** something is done a certain way
- Document APIs, complex algorithms, and non-obvious side effects

## Single Responsibility

- Each function should do exactly one thing
- Functions should be small and focused
- If a function needs a comment to explain what it does, it should be split

## DRY

- Extract repeated logic into helpers under `src/lib/` (or colocated module helpers)
- Share common logic through proper abstraction
- Maintain single sources of truth (types in `src/types/`, schema in `supabase/migrations/`)

## Clean Structure

- Keep related code together (`components/`, `lib/`, `app/` routes)
- Use consistent file and folder naming (kebab-case files, PascalCase components)

## CSS / Tailwind — Mobile-first

- **Base styles target the smallest viewport.** Add larger layouts with `sm:` / `md:` / `lg:` (min-width), never desktop-first patched by max-width overrides.
- Progressive enhancement: single column and large tap targets first; sidebars and toolbars at `md+`.
- Prefer existing CSS variables in `globals.css` (`--accent`, `--border`, etc.) over one-off hex values.

## Encapsulation

- Hide implementation details; expose clear interfaces
- Move nested conditionals into well-named functions

## Code Quality Maintenance

- Refactor continuously; leave code cleaner than you found it
- Fix technical debt early when touching related code

## Testing

- Write tests before fixing bugs when practical
- Keep tests readable; cover edge cases and error conditions

## Version Control

- Clear commit messages; small focused commits; meaningful branch names (`feat/`, `fix/`, `chore/`)
